Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:05:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(hud): retain server visibility restrictions

Decode SetHud packet 308 into per-element restrictions for Bedrock 1.26.51 protocol 2193. Target BDS captures establish the unsigned array length, signed enum varints, all thirteen element IDs, and hide/reset values.

Retain independent updates and transport a versioned snapshot after Java joins and late channel registration. Reset removes server restrictions without changing the player's local visibility settings. Preserve unknown element IDs across updates and transport. Bound malformed arrays before allocation.

Java has no standard packet for individual HUD visibility. Core owns decoding, state, and ViaProxy transport; registered clients apply the restrictions during HUD rendering. Ordinary Java clients retain the authoritative state without receiving unsupported custom payloads.
